    "finalPromptText": "I'm working on a close-reading essay for my French literature course on Madame Bovary by Gustave Flaubert. My professor wants us to analyze how Flaubert uses free indirect discourse in the early chapters — specifically the scenes where Emma is at the Vaubyessard ball. I need to look at how the narrative voice blends with Emma's consciousness in those passages. Could you help me find the relevant sections from Part One and show me how Flaubert's prose style shifts between the narrator's perspective and Emma's interiority? I have access to the novel through my university library but I'm struggling to pinpoint the exact moments where the technique is most evident.",
